# Database Rules

## Schema
Four tables: `analyses`, `agent_runs`, `checkpoints`, `agent_improvements`.
Read the Data Schema section of `design.md` before any DB work.

## Never Do These
- NEVER write raw SQL inline in application code — all queries go in `backend/database/queries.py`
- NEVER use f-strings or string concatenation in SQL — always parameterised queries
- NEVER create a new table without a corresponding migration file in `backend/database/migrations/`
- NEVER skip logging to `agent_runs` — every agent run must have a start and end record

## Always Do These
- New table → new numbered migration file (`002_`, `003_` etc.)
- Every agent run logged: `agent_name`, `started_at`, `completed_at`, `token_count`, `tool_calls_count`
- Checkpoint saved immediately after Lead Orchestrator planning completes
- `last_completed_agent` updated in `analyses` table after each agent finishes — enables resume on failure

## Resume on Failure
- Pipeline reads `last_completed_agent` on restart and skips completed agents
- NEVER restart pipeline from scratch — always resume from checkpoint
- Partial outputs from completed agents are preserved in DB for debugging
